          "text": "The team ran some tests, including:\n- Blood tests\n- A urine test\n- An ultrasound scan of your tummy\n\nThe scan showed some free fluid on the right side of your tummy. The histology (tissue test) result is still pending.\n\nWhile you were in hospital, the team:\n- Gave you fluids through a drip\n- Gave you an antibiotic (co-amoxiclav) through a drip\n- Performed an operation to remove your appendix (laparoscopic appendicectomy)\n\nDuring the operation, the appendix was found to be acutely inflamed. There was no perforation. The operation was uncomplicated and blood loss was minimal.\n\nAbsorbable stitches were used. You do not need to have them removed."
